    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0575" n="477" xml:id="pg477"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr.
                            Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 783.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s reply of the
                    19th ultimo to your dispatch No. 654, of April 3 last, concerning the towing of
                    the disabled French steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Bretagne</hi> into the
                    port of Bahia by the United States cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Chicago</hi>,
                    I inclose for communication to the “Société Générate de Transports Maritimes á
                    Vapeur” at Paris a copy of a letter from the Secretary of the Navy reporting
                    that a copy of your abovementioned dispatch with its accompanying papers had
                    been forwarded to Rear-Admiral W. S. Schley, U. S. N.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi><lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d573-a1.xml" xpointer="d573-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
